  "vendor_website": "solaxpower.com",
  "revision": 5,
  "revised": "2026-11-15",
  "source": "SolaX Power, Hybrid X1 & X3 G4 Modbus TCP & RTU communication protocol, V3.29",
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on RS-485, default station address 1, 19200 8N1. The inverter has no Modbus TCP of its own; TCP on port 502 comes from SolaX's monitoring module. Poll no faster than once per second, with at least 1 s between two requests.",
    "Only the real-time values of function 04 (input registers) are mapped. The settings registers of function 03 (read) and 06/16 (write) are not mapped.",
    "Addresses are those printed in the manual in hexadecimal; address base 0. Register values are big-endian; the manual says 32-bit values use little-endian order, so the low word is at the lower address (word order little).",
    "Names ending in (X1) or (X3) apply to that family only; the manual does not say what the other family returns there. The X1-AC is taken to follow the X1 columns; the manual's title names the Hybrid X1 and X3 G4 only.",
    "Three registers (0x9A, 0xAE, 0xB0) are listed in the manual as 16-bit values with a length of two registers; they are mapped as 32-bit, low word first, like their neighbours.",
    "The document used here is V3.29 (the cover page reads V3.28), a copy of the manufacturer's protocol hosted on a public forum, because SolaX hands the current file out on request.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
